Running the Android app (install, launch, UI checks, screenshots) goes through Google's Android CLI
(`android emulator start`, `android install`, `android run --device <serial>`, `android layout`,
`android screen capture`), not adb — adb only lists devices and sends input taps / typing, which the
CLI lacks — see [testing.md § Running on a device or emulator](https://github.com/arthurnagy/kmp-forge/blob/main/docs/testing.md#running-on-a-device-or-emulator).
Use an emulator for ad-hoc runs; never install to a physical device without asking first. To check a
change against its acceptance scenarios on a device (journeys + screenshots), ask for the `kmp-qa`
agent after `/opsx:apply` — it may use a connected phone, touching only the app under test.

Prefer kmp-forge slash commands over hand-rolled scaffolding:
`/kmp-forge-add-feature`, `/kmp-forge-add-screen`, `/kmp-forge-add-platform`, `/kmp-forge-add-library`, `/kmp-forge-bump-stack`, `/kmp-forge-spec`, `/kmp-forge-groom`, `/kmp-forge-doctor`, `/kmp-forge-add-autoloop`.

